forcal_picker_demo_live = Try it
forcal_picker_demo_intro = The forCal picker turns an ordinary text field into a selection of events, categories or venues. The class forcal-picker is all it takes. The widget loads on every backend page, so it works in modules, MForm, MBlock, YForm, rex_form and your own HTML. The code to copy is on the right, the stored value below.
forcal_picker_demo_value = Stored value:
forcal_picker_demo_entry = One event
forcal_picker_demo_entry_text = For “our next highlight”. If you cannot find the event, create it right in the dialog with “Create new”.
forcal_picker_demo_entries = Several events, at most 6, online only
forcal_picker_demo_entries_text = For hand-picked event lists. Order by drag and drop or with Alt + arrow key.
forcal_picker_demo_category = Categories
forcal_picker_demo_category_text = For modules that output upcoming events of certain categories.
forcal_picker_demo_venue = One venue
forcal_picker_demo_venue_text = For directions pages or “all events at this venue”.
forcal_picker_demo_past = Including past events
forcal_picker_demo_past_text = The dialog starts with the latest events. Good for reviews.
forcal_picker_demo_clone = Repeater test
forcal_picker_demo_clone_text = MBlock and the MForm repeater copy finished markup and then trigger rex:ready. The button does exactly that. Every copy must be an independent widget: change the copy and the original stays as it is.
forcal_picker_demo_clone_label = Events
forcal_picker_demo_clone_button = Clone row
forcal_picker_demo_api = JavaScript API
forcal_picker_demo_api_text = The dialog can also be opened without an input field. ForcalPicker.create() opens just the quick-create form, as in the calendar.
forcal_picker_demo_api_create = Open quick create
